    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d141">

                <pb facs="0277" n="183" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg183"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">813.01/A: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in El Salvador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Robbins</hi>)<anchor n="6"
                        xml:id="d141-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-12-20T20:00:00-05:00">December 20, 1930—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>31. The Department has today advised the Legation at Guatemala City that this
                    Government supports the 1923 Treaties. The Legation was instructed to advise
                    informally and orally the Guatemalan authorities that this Government’s policy
                    in the recognition of new Governments in Central America is as stated by Mr.
                    Hughes on June 30, 1923 and as reaffirmed by the Secretary on September 17 last.
                    While the Department does not desire to make a public statement <pb facs="0278"
                        n="184" xml:id="pg184"/> at this time, it desires you to make known its
                    position in conversation with the officials of the Government and other
                    political leaders of the country to which you are accredited.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d141-f1" n="6" type="source" xml:id="d141-f1-content">
                <p>The same on the same date to the diplomatic missions in Costa Rica (34), Honduras
                    (93), and Nicaragua (137).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
